{
  "name": "hold_fwd",
  "note": "(anim-rework S6 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced; M5) Holding a guard, a slow push forward: short steps of about 26 cm, heel first and rolled, knees soft (14-28 deg), the trunk 2 deg further forward than the hold and the pelvis 1 cm further back (her chest leans onto him), so she drives him with her chest and hips; feet near hip width (add 0.5), the arms on the hold contacts. Not mirrored (8 keys: the hands keep their sides). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in); wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. The arms were solved onto the guard's contacts (his clips posed at the game's hold placement: 0.32 m ahead, 0.1 m to her left, his 1.78 m against her 1.68 m) and written as plain angles: edit these numbers directly. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
